cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Sesiidae Pheromone Atlas, cite the tagged release you used
  and the IDs of the records you relied on (spa.obs....), and cite the
  original paper behind each record: the Atlas does not replace it. No
  release has been tagged and no DOI minted yet; until then, cite the
  repository and the commit.
type: dataset
title: "Sesiidae Pheromone Atlas"
abstract: >-
  A curated, machine-readable resource on clearwing-moth (Sesiidae)
  pheromones. Observation-level records from primary full texts keep female
  chemistry, male behaviour and antennal responses apart, each with its
  experimental context (sample material, lure purity, trap, dispenser), and
  are linked to atom-mapped compound structures and genome assemblies.
authors:
  - given-names: Thanakrit
    family-names: Wongsatit
    alias: Austin
repository-code: "https://github.com/Azuromalachite/sesiidae-pheromone-atlas"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - Sesiidae
  - clearwing moths
  - sex pheromones
  - chemical ecology
  - curated dataset
version: 0.1.0-dev
